Article 22 Where a medical dispute occurs, the medical practitioner and the patient may resolve it through the following channels:
(1) voluntary negotiation between the two parties;
(2) applying for people's mediation;
(3) applying for administrative mediation;
(4) initiating prosecution with the People's Court;
(5) other channels provided by laws and regulations.

Article 23 Where a medical dispute occurs, the medical institution shall inform the patient or his or her close relatives of the following matters:
(1) the lawful channels for resolving the medical dispute;
(2) the provisions on sealing and unsealing of relevant medical records and on-site physical evidence;
(3) the provisions on viewing and copying of relevant medical records.
If the patient dies, the medical institution shall also inform his or her close relatives of the provisions on autopsy.

Article 36 The medical damage appraisal opinion issued by a medical association or a forensic appraisal institution shall contain and discuss in detail the following contents:
(1) whether there is medical damage and the degree of damage;
(2) whether there is a medical fault;
(3) whether there is a causal relationship between the medical fault and the medical damage;
(4) the degree of liability of the medical fault in the medical damage.

Article 37 Where consulting experts or appraisal personnel fall under any of the following circumstances, they shall withdraw, and the party may also apply for their withdrawal orally or in writing:
(1) they are a party to the medical dispute or a close relative of a party;
(2) they have an interest in the medical dispute;
(3) they have other relationships with a party to the medical dispute that may affect the fair handling of the medical dispute.

Article 47 Where a medical institution or its medical personnel commits any of the following acts, the health competent authority of the people's government at or above the county level shall order rectification, give a warning, and impose a fine of not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 50,000 yuan; where the circumstances are serious, the health competent authority shall impose or order the imposition of a sanction of demotion or dismissal upon the directly responsible person in charge and other directly liable persons, and may order the suspension of the practice activities of the relevant medical personnel for not less than one month but not more than six months; where a crime is constituted, criminal liability shall be investigated according to law:
(1) failing to formulate and implement a medical quality and safety management system as required;
(2) failing to inform the patient of the condition, medical measures, medical risks, alternative treatment options, etc., as required;
(3) carrying out diagnosis and treatment activities with relatively high medical risks without preparing response plans in advance to prevent sudden risks;
(4) failing to fill in and keep medical records as required, or failing to supplement the rescue records as required;
(5) refusing to provide services for the patient to consult or copy medical records;
(6) failing to establish a complaint reception system, set up a unified complaint management department, or assign full-time (or part-time) personnel;
(7) failing to seal, keep, or unseal medical records and on-site physical evidence as required;
(8) failing to report a major medical dispute to the health competent authority as required;
(9) other circumstances of failing to perform the obligations provided in these Regulations.

Article 50 Where a people's mediator for medical dispute commits any of the following acts, the Medical Dispute People's Mediation Committee shall give criticism and education, and order rectification; where the circumstances are serious, the mediator shall be dismissed according to law:
(1) favoring one party;
(2) insulting a party;
(3) extorting or accepting property or seeking other improper benefits;
(4) disclosing matters such as the personal privacy of the medical and patient parties.
